                                text "Scope landed: added ImplementationType::is_weighted() (true for TROPICAL_OPENFST/LOG_OPENFST/HFST_OLW) in hfst_data_types.rs and used it for hfst-fst2txt's weighting clause. Added tests/test_implementation_type.rs (weighted vs unweighted variants). 130 lib tests + OL golden green; fst2txt prints the weight column on a tropical fst.\n\nGrounding corrected the node premise (which said \"HfstTransducer::is_weighted() already exists — call it\"): the FACADE HfstTransducer has NO is_weighted (only the hfst-ol Transducer does), and the C++ HfstTransducer has none either — C++ fst2txt.cc uses the same bespoke per-type branching. So this is a new lib predicate, not a pre-existing call.\n\nBehavior-preservation proof: fst2txt's chain is `SFST/FOMA/XFSM -> false; TROPICAL/LOG -> true; else -> true`. Because the else arm ALSO yields true, the decision collapses to printw = !(SFST|FOMA|XFSM). Replacing the TROPICAL||LOG clause condition with type_.is_weighted() (which adds HFST_OLW) is byte-identical: HFST_OLW was already caught by else->true, every other type lands in the same arm as before. Documented inline at the call site."
